  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How the terms nest",
      "items": [
        "A machine gives an environment: terra is local, sol is remote, and a cloud environment has no machine you can name",
        "An agent host runs harnesses and owns their sessions; clients come and go",
        "An agent is a model working through a harness; a session is one run of it",
        "Subagent threads sit inside the session, subordinate to its agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Other agent hosts",
      "items": [
        "Claude Desktop, ChatGPT desktop, the Antigravity app, VS Code Agent Host",
        "Codex in a terminal is host and client in one, like claude"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Reading it",
      "items": [
        "One client can view several hosts: the Orca app sees terra and sol",
        "One program can be host and client: Orca.app, claude in a terminal",
        "The phone can also reach claude in a terminal by Remote Control",
        "Skills load into any session by progressive disclosure, so they are not drawn",
        "sol's session and the cloud row are illustrative"
      ]
    }
  ]
